    {
      "id": "r2",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 87. वितीर्ण—given away; p. p. of तॄ with वि. तरुण–young,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "tender. विगुण &c.—having an unfortunate result. विधिगतीः–the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "motions i. e. the workings of fate. त्रियामा–the night. त्रियामा क्षणदा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "क्षपा Amara. याम is a prahara or 3 hours ( द्वौ यामप्रहरौ समौ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "Amara ); and the night is considered to have only three pra-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "haras, the first half watch and the last half watch being ex-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "cluded. शरण—a protector, saviour.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 88. वाराणसी Benares. त्रिपुरहर—this alludes to the story",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "of the three Puras or towns of the demons, of gold, silver, and",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "iron, situated in the sky, air and on earth, and built for them",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "by Maya, which were burnt down by S'iva along with the de-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "mons inhabiting them. See Kum. VII. 48. आक्रोशन्—merely",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "means here–loudly–uttering.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 89. ध्येय—( i. e. You ) who deserve to be contemplated.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "क्षितिधर &c.—There does not seem to be any propriety of मूले ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "आत्मारामः—finding delight in self ( i. e. in the contemplation of",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "the self or Brahma ). समकरचरणो–On this Râmarshi observes सम-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "करचरणो ( मकरेण सहितौ समकरौ चरणौ यस्य ) हि पुमान् धनवान्भवतीति",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "सामुद्रिके प्रसिद्धम् । मत्स्यांकितचरणो हि पुमान् धनवान् भवतीत्यपि ।",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "ध्यानमार्गैक &c v. l —ध्यानस्य मार्गः, तद्विषयक एकः केवलः प्रश्नो यस्य",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "सः । his only inquiry being that touching the method of con-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "templation. This reading, however, violates the metre.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 90 एकाकी—एकः एव अकति गच्छतीति going alone in the",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "world. पाणिपात्रः—to whom his hand is serviceable like a pot.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "कर्मनिर्मूलन—destroying entirely the roots. This is essential to",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "cut off the repetition of births and deaths. This is done by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "being संगरहित as indicated in the first half. Samsàra is here",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "compared to a tree of which actions are the roots. Cf. अश्वत्थ-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "मेनं सुविरूढमूलमसंगशस्त्रेण दृढेन छित्वा । Bhg. XV. 3; also S'árîraka",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "Bhàshya on Brah. Sû. IV. 1. 14. 19.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Sl. 91. पात्रय्—a denom. भैक्षम्-भिक्षयत इति what is obtained by",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "alms; fr. भिक्ष्+अ. बहुत्तृणम्—a little short of, almost equal to,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "grass; see com. तृणकल्पमित्यर्थः । ‘विभाषा सुपौ बहुच् पुरस्तात्तु Pán,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "V. 3. 68. ईषदसमाप्तिविशिष्टेऽर्थे सुबन्तात् बहुच् ( the prefix बहु ) वा",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "स्यात्स च प्रागेव ( prefixed ) न तु परतः । ईषदूनः पटुः बहुपटुः &c. Sid.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    }
  ],
